turboexl3_qwen38 vendors third-party code, each part unchanged but for the edits scripts/sync-mlx-serve.sh makes and
names. It is built against the mlx-serve plugin kit and turboexl3 (build.zig.zon, by URL and hash).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mlx-serve
https://github.com/ddalcu/mlx-serve
Copyright (c) 2026 David Dalcu
Licensed under the MIT License.

src/mlx_serve/ holds the slice of mlx-serve's src/ this plugin runs (scripts/slice.txt), at the paths it has there, from
the commit in src/mlx_serve/MLX_SERVE_COMMIT (the head of ddalcu/mlx-serve#1005), with the Metal kernels it embeds. The
slice is the files that hold code the plugin's builds compile (the dylib, `zig build test`, mlx-free-test and gpu-test),
found from those builds' symbols and the compiler's errors. The script's edits: each file's `copied_from` line; the
imports of what the kit ships, pointed at the kit; mlx-c handles default-initialised with their one field; `pub` on six
functions of plugins/qwen4_exp/plugin.zig and on its model's `ownSlot`; and abi/quant.zig with the declarations the
kit's quant ABI has unchanged re-exported from the kit; and the kernel contract's registry
(sdk/testing/kernel_contract/registry.zig) with its `areas` cut to those whose kernels this plugin ships. A `stand_in`
file is an empty one for an import whose code no build compiles: Zig loads every file a file imports. The script's cut
edges (its EDGES list) are this plugin's own code, not copies; one of them, engines/mlx/generate/generator.zig, declares
the fields of mlx-serve's Generator that the copied MTP round policy (engines/mlx/spec/mtp/) reads, with their types and
defaults, and names the copies' own methods.

